    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0730" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/7–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in France
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d277-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-01T17:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2381. For Martin from Gay. MFN Japan. Dept agrees
                    that to press for detailed negots may be impractical in time available but in
                    view action taken Brussels<anchor n="2" xml:id="d277-f2"/> Dept believes <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoires</hi> should be presented Paris. Due
                    special problem NEI presentation Hague shld be
                        postponed.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d277-f3"/> (Urtel 292 June 29) At all four capitals you should: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Push ahead with discussions top civil servants and ministerial level
                            if possible to give maximum emphasis importance US attaches to
                            question.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Discuss concrete agreement, using Annex 1 as basis, and possible
                            provisions to meet their problems.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d277-f4"/>
                        </item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Urge that answers to <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoires</hi>
                            (except at Hague) receive full cabinet review and not be handled in
                            routine fashion.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Explore proper timing bringing issue to head in Cabinets at same time
                            making clear US intends continue press for satisfactory
                            agreement.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Re your Para 3 last sentence,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d277-f5"/> some explanation
                    basis US objectives probably desirable, turning emphasis on importance peaceful,
                    well integrated Jap. Re Para 1 <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi> and Para 4
                    believed wise avoiding encouraging prolonged postponement.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d277-f6"/> [Gay.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d277-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d277-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Annecy (269), Brussels (811), The Hague (578), and London (2276).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f2" n="2" xml:id="d277-f2-content">
                <p>The Embassy at Brussels had presented the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> to the Belgian Ministry for Foreign Affairs on June 30,
                    prior to receiving Annecy’s telegram 292 to the Department, June 29, 5 p. m.
                    (telegram 933, from Brussels, June 30, not printed, 560.AL/6–3049)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f3" n="3" xml:id="d277-f3-content">
                <p>This point had been emphasized again by the Embassy at The Hague in its telegram
                    554, June 30, 4 p. m. The Embassy had cited other economic factors also as
                    boding “serious resistance in obtaining assurances” from the Netherlands
                    Government, and cautioning that “US may have to resort largely to political
                    arguments.” (560.AL/6–3049)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f4" n="3" xml:id="d277-f4-content">
                <p>This point had been emphasized again by the Embassy at The Hague in its telegram
                    554, June 30, 4 p. m. The Embassy had cited other economic factors also as
                    boding “serious resistance in obtaining assurances” from the Netherlands
                    Government, and cautioning that “US may have to resort largely to political
                    arguments.” (560.AL/6–3049)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f5" n="4" xml:id="d277-f5-content">
                <p>Refers to the draft agreement.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f6" n="5" xml:id="d277-f6-content">
                <p>References in this paragraph are to numbered paragraphs in Annecy’s 292, June 29,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
